Keeps `data/` present in the Docker build context.

The Dockerfile copies `data/.keep data/hillbomb-deploy.gol* ./data/` so that the
GOL is optional — an image built without one still works, falling back to
Overpass for every search. A Docker glob that matches zero files is a build
error, so this file guarantees at least one match.

It is deliberately not a `.md`: both .dockerignore and .gcloudignore exclude
`*.md`, so a Markdown sentinel is absent from the build context exactly when the
COPY needs it. See data/README.md for what actually goes in this directory.
